{%- comment -%}
  ci-profile-banner.liquid — global taste-profile ribbon.
  Shown ONLY on the Shop + shelf pages, and ONLY when a taste profile exists
  (visibility + state driven by updateRibbon/renderRibbon in ci-storefront.js).
  Toggles taste filtering on/off; "Edit profile" opens the taste console modal.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div class="taste-ribbon" id="taste-ribbon">
  <div class="flag-strip taste-ribbon-flag" aria-hidden="true"><div></div><div></div><div></div></div>
  <div class="taste-ribbon-inner">
    <div class="tr-main">
      <span class="tr-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <p class="tr-status" id="tr-status"></p>
      <div class="profile-tags tr-tags" id="tr-tags"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="tr-actions">
      {%- comment -%}
        Shown to signed-OUT visitors only (renderRibbon toggles it). This is where the
        account ask lives now: AFTER the quiz result has proven useful, not before it.
        POC12 removed the sign-in gate that used to sit at the quiz payoff.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        "Edit profile" used to be a third control here. It now lives inside the status
        sentence as a link on the word "profile" (see renderRibbon) - a third control
        pushed the actions onto two rows on every phone, and burying the edit in the
        text is what gets the whole ribbon back to one row without shrinking any label.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <button class="tr-save" id="tr-save" onclick="saveProfileFromRibbon()" hidden>Save to my account</button>
      <button class="tr-toggle" id="tr-toggle" onclick="toggleProfileFilter()">Apply profile</button>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
